  "_readme": [
    "EDITABLE BENCHMARK DATASET — tune these freely, then re-run `npm run seed` (or",
    "use the admin API: GET/POST /api/benchmarks) to load them.",
    "",
    "Each row defines a reference value the rating engine compares athletes against.",
    "Matching precedence (most specific wins): sport+position+sex > sport+sex > sex > generic.",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  metricKey   – must match a MetricType.key",
    "  sport       – null applies to all sports; else 'Basketball', 'Soccer', 'Football', ...",
    "  position    – null applies to all positions; else 'Guard', 'Big', 'Skill', 'Lineman', ...",
    "  sex         – 'M' | 'F' | null (both)",
    "  level       – 'ELITE' | 'GOOD' | 'AVERAGE'",
    "  mean, sd    – population mean and standard deviation (sd enables z-scores)",
    "  unitsNote   – the unit the mean is expressed in (e.g. 'cm', 's', 'xBodyweight')",
    "  source      – citation",
    "  confidence  – 'HIGH' | 'MEDIUM' | 'LOW' (surfaced in the UI; LOW = treat as estimate)",
    "  notes       – caveats (protocol, population, etc.)",
    "",
    "NOTE: back_squat_1rm means are in xBodyweight because that metric is rated",
    "relative to bodyweight. All others are in the metric's native unit.",
    "These are DRAFT values pending Rod's review — adjust before relying on ratings."
